<title>FRANCE: Analysts raise Alcatel forecasts.</title>
<headline>Analysts raise Alcatel forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial analysts have raised their 1996 and 1997 profit forecasts for Alcatel Alsthom following the government's decision to sell Thomson SA to Lagardere Groupe and not to Alcatel.</p>
<p>According to a poll by Jacques Chahine Finance, analysts on average see 1996 earnings per share for Alcatel of 8.40 francs, rising to 27.30 francs in 1997.</p>
<p>Last week, before the government announcement but after the first half results, analysts expected 1996 earnings per share of 8.20 francs rising to 26.80 in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
